        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T17:59:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are a few things to clean up here:\n1. `switch` statements on `pdc_state_t` variables that are now incomplete, e.g in `should_suspend`, should have an additional or defualt case.\n2. Arrays indexed by `pdc_state_t` should have another element, e.g. `pdc_state_names`.",
      "parentUuid": "cac42990_3c8eb972",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "e690d390ed2064a6e80d9e5a47a73f9d5529a07b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afd6baae_da0c3b54",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/usbc/pdc_power_mgmt.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1524179
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T03:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For 1., I think line 874 in `pdc_power_mgmt.c` should meet our need? Supposedly, the `PDC_INVALID` is only used for `send_cmd_return_state`, so in that switch statment, we would like to treat the `PDC_INVALID` as an invalid state if that value appears in `current_state`.\nFor 2., updated.",
      "parentUuid": "c0bb49c2_7179e3c2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "e690d390ed2064a6e80d9e5a47a73f9d5529a07b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0eea6823_61f92af7",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/usbc/pdc_power_mgmt.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T21:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "874 is `case PDC_STATE_COUNT:`, a different value than `PDC_INVALID`. You could make the case that each value would ultimately result in an assertion failure, but they\u0027re different assertion failures. I don\u0027t think there\u0027s any advantage to leaving this behavior implicit.\n\nI think it would suffice to replace the `case PDC_STATE_COUNT:` with `default:`, which would cover both of the values under discussion.",
      "parentUuid": "afd6baae_da0c3b54",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "e690d390ed2064a6e80d9e5a47a73f9d5529a07b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aed55c38_82633a74",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/usbc/pdc_power_mgmt.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1524179
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-13T05:38:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, I think it is a good thing to be explicit, but I do not support using `default:` here. I actually benefit from not having the `default:`, because the compiller explicitly pointed out that I missed handling that case here. If someone in the future found they need to add more enum here, the `default:` case would siliently include that case, leaving a pit hole for them.\n\nAs such, I prefer not to use the `default:` here, but use another assertion with a more clean and explicit reason here.",
      "parentUuid": "0eea6823_61f92af7",
